{"name":"Brain Freeze","hex":"#00eeff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brain freeze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pain in the head from eating or drinking something cold; a cold-stimulus headache.","Failure to remember something, with the sense that recall is imminent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brain_freeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brain Freeze (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Brain Freeze is a 2021 French-Canadian horror comedy film, written, directed, and scored by Julien Knafo."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Brain_freeze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_Freeze_(film)","wikidata":"Q107439259"},{"title":"Cold-stimulus headache","blocks":[{"text":"A cold-stimulus headache, colloquially known as an ice-cream headache or brain freeze, is a form of brief pain or headache, commonly associated with consumption of cold beverages or foods such as ice cream, popsicles, slushies, and snow cones. It is caused by a cold substance touching the roof of the mouth, and is believed to result from a nerve response causing rapid constriction and swelling of blood vessels, \"referring\" pain from the roof of the mouth to the head. The rate of intake for cold foods has been studied as a contributing factor. It can also occur during a sudden exposure of the unprotected head to low temperatures, such as by diving into cold water. A cold-stimulus headache is distinct from dentin hypersensitivity, a type of dental pain that can occur under similar circumstances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg/330px-Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold-stimulus_headache","wikidata":"Q284967"},{"title":"Brain","blocks":[{"text":"The brain is an organ that serves as the center of the nervous system in all vertebrate and most invertebrate animals. It consists of nervous tissue and is typically located in the head (cephalization), usually near organs for special senses such as vision, hearing, and olfaction. Being the most specialized organ, it is responsible for receiving information from the sensory nervous system, processing that information and the coordination of motor control and the endocrine system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Chimp_Brain_in_a_jar.jpg/330px-Chimp_Brain_in_a_jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain","wikidata":"Q1073"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Brain_freeze.jpg/250px-Brain_freeze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Brain_freeze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Brain_freeze.jpg/250px-Brain_freeze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrain_freeze.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg/500px-Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg/1280px-Girl_with_Ice_Cream_-_Southend-on-Sea_-_Essex_-_England_%2827713936233%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thu